    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1125">

                <pb facs="1411" n="1401" xml:id="pg1401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.52/10–2447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-24T18:00:00+09:00">October 24, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:39 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2135. Foreign Office and Ministry Land Administration have both indicated
                    informal approval draft press release of October 7, 1947 (Department’s telegram
                    1236, repeated Shanghai as 1708) concerning re-registration real property rights
                    Shanghai. Please inform Embassy date of release.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d1125-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 2135, repeated Shanghai as 854.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1125-f1" n="30" xml:id="d1125-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 1320, October 30, 5 p.m. (893.52/10–3047), the Department
                    informed the Embassy that the press release had been issued on October 28,
                    thereby extending the re-registration deadline to April 28, 1948; for press
                    release, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, November
                    9, 1947, p. 916.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
